Oracle authorization:71048fd8-1e65-45de-b2c5-8c4c9f1498b4.
Host measured 2026-10-22: macOS27.0.1, Apple M4/Metal, Chrome156.0.8078.48.

Mechanism:
crates/bbt-ui/src/style.rs:354 — Text.italic defaults false, omitted when false
  from serialized Style records, so existing documents retain their shape.
crates/bbt-ui-model/src/layout/solve.rs:9 — measurement carries the same flag.
crates/bbt-ui-model/src/draw/prim.rs:102 — retained draw text carries the flag.
crates/bbt-ui/src/components.rs:1453 — resolved Text passes italic into paint;
  measurement and bboxybook font adapters carry it too, not just raster paint.
crates/bbt-render/src/chrome/text.rs:67 — upright requests return through the
  original font path. Italic requests normalized numeric slant0.2 + italic bit;
  a same-family symbolic lookup handles discrete families ignoring numeric slant.
  UI wght is reapplied exactly. Synthetic oblique is used only if both lookups
  find no real italic. No terminal font/cell path was edited.
crates/bbt-render/src/chrome/text.rs:323 — face/matrix/weight/coverage and
  backing-scale regression. Actual names on this host:
  UI weights400/500/600/700: .SFNS-RegularItalic, wght400/500/600/700,
  angle12.5°, identity matrix. Menlo400/500: Menlo-Italic;600/700:
  Menlo-BoldItalic, angle-11°, identity matrix. No synthetic slant was used.
  Chrome reports the same italic family; its700 face name is .SFNS-BoldItalic.
crates/bbt-ui/tests/italic.rs — old JSON reads false, true roundtrips and
  reaches measurement and emitted draw records.

